supermox-ve (0.1.19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * init.d/supermox-cgroups: new service script. LXC containers could not start
    on our nodes: lxc-pve 7.x is built for cgroup v2 only and nothing in the
    sysvinit boot sequence mounts a cgroup hierarchy at /sys/fs/cgroup, so
    `pct start` died with "Failed to receive the container state". The script
    mounts the unified cgroup2 hierarchy, delegates the controllers LXC and
    QEMU resource limits need, and is enabled so it runs in rcS.d right after
    mountkernfs, before lxcfs and the PVE services.
  * init.d/supermox-wg: `up` and `conf` now sync the routing table as well as
    the keys. wg syncconf never touches routes, so a member added after the
    interface came up was listed by `wg show` and unreachable in fact ("Network
    is unreachable"); routes of members that left the cluster are removed too.
  * Pairs with pve-cluster 9.1.7+supermox2, whose init script seeds
    /etc/pve/storage.cfg: a clean node had no storage defined at all, so
    `pct create` and the web UI's Create CT failed with
    "volume 'local:...' does not exist".

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 05:50:46 -0800

supermox-ve (0.1.18) unstable; urgency=medium

  * init.d/supermox-joind: `start` on a node that has no cluster yet exits 0
    with a "no cluster here; run supermox-join create" message instead of
    failing. The daemon itself refuses to run without cluster state, so the
    old start path made a fresh node's boot report a failed service and left
    no pidfile; the service is now a no-op until a cluster exists. An unreadable
    (present but corrupt) state file still starts the daemon, so a damaged
    cluster is reported rather than silently ignored.
  * supermox-join create: creating a cluster now writes /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf
    and starts the WireGuard overlay, exactly like `join` and `conf` already
    did. Before, a freshly created cluster had no tunnel until someone ran
    `conf`, so the first node of a new cluster could not be reached.
  * Pairs with pve-firewall 6.0.6+supermox2, whose init script no longer pins
    the iptables family to the legacy backend (f10d-1: our kernels have no
    legacy ebtables bridge module, so pve-firewall logged a status update
    error every 10 seconds).

