supermox-ve (0.1.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depend on isc-dhcp-client (>= 4.4.3-P1-8+supermox1): pve-container pulls
    isc-dhcp-client in for /sbin/dhclient (host-managed container networks),
    but Devuan Ceres does not ship it, and the Debian build's client package
    installs dhclient hooks that call the service manager to feed leases to
    systemd-resolved. We fork isc-dhcp (patches/isc-dhcp) to drop those hooks
    and disable the debhelper unit-install step, and this versioned dependency
    makes apt pick our fork instead of any other copy. Only the client and its
    isc-dhcp-common manpages are pulled in; the server, relay, keama, dev and
    ddns packages built from the same source are not dependencies and stay out
    of the ISO.

