supermox-ve (0.1.14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship init.d/rrdcached and enable it at boot: Debian installs rrdcached with
    only a systemd unit, and upstream pve-cluster.service pulls it in with
    Wants=rrdcached.service, so under sysvinit nothing ever started it. PVE's
    PVE::RRD talks to unix:/var/run/rrdcached.sock, which Debian gets from
    systemd socket activation, so the script passes -l /var/run/rrdcached.sock
    (and -p /run/rrdcached.pid) on top of the unit's -B -b/-j arguments from
    /etc/default/rrdcached; -g is dropped because the daemon has to fork.
    Without it the RRD archives pvestatd files stay empty and the graphs page
    has no history. config/init-scripts.txt lists the new script, and rrdcached
    is now an explicit dependency.

